# The build context holds only what the Dockerfile copies: backend/ and
# web/. Everything else stays out, e.g. .git, local .env files, and editor
# folders.
*
!backend/
!web/

# Inside those, leave out what each machine makes for itself: installed
# packages, build output, binaries, and caches. The Dockerfile builds them.
**/node_modules
**/dist
backend/bin
backend/tmp
**/.cache
**/*.log

# Local settings, possibly secrets.
**/.env*
